      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a4f02d7f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts three children with traditional tribal adornments, likely from an African ethnic group, juxtaposed with the text 'when you have 3 choco puffs left in your cereal bowl.' This creates a harmful and demeaning stereotype by equating the children with a childish, impoverished, or primitive state, implying they are 'leftover' or 'waste' like the last few cereal pieces. The visual of the children, who are presented with dignity and cultural pride, is used to mock a mundane, everyday situation, reducing their humanity to a joke. This is a form of racial stereotyping that dehumanizes and infantilizes Black children, fitting under the 'Hateful' category as it is a direct attack on a specific racial group based on protected characteristics. The meme's intent is to provoke laughter through a degrading comparison, which is inherently harmful and offensive.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b64b4f83"
      },
